Here's my research on Spanish Olive Oil yesterday.


Spain produces nearly half of the world's olive oil, with 75% originating
in Andalusia, particularly Ja=C3=A9n. The supply chain operates as a vast
network spanning roughly 2.5 million hectares. It moves from massive
agricultural cooperatives and advanced milling facilities through to global
export networks. [1
<https://www.shop.bottegadelsarto.com/feed/global-olive-oil-supply-chain-ch=
allenges-776804>,
2 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>, 3
<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DMoPqPsebq28&t=3D1>, 4
<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive_oil>, 5
<https://oliveoilsfromspain.org/industry/>]
1. Agriculture & Harvesting

   - *Cultivation:* Spain has over 340 million olive trees. The growing,
   maintenance, and harvesting are heavily managed by agricultural engineer=
s.
   [1 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>, 2
   <https://oliveoilsfromspain.org/industry/>]
   - *Harvest Season:* Olives are primarily harvested from November to
   January. [1 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>]
   - *Mechanization:* Modern groves utilize advanced shaking machinery (
   *vibradoras*) to efficiently harvest olives without damaging the trees
   or the fruit. [1 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>]

2. Milling & Processing (*Almazaras*)

   - *Milling:* Harvested olives are sent to local mills. Spain contains
   over 1,700 active oil mills, including the world=E2=80=99s largest mill =
located in
   Villacarrillo (Ja=C3=A9n), which can process up to 2,500 tonnes of olive=
s per
   day. [1 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive_oil>, 2
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>, 3
   <https://oliveoilsfromspain.org/industry/>, 4
   <https://www.foodswinesfromspain.com/en/food/products/olive-oil>]
   - *Extraction:* Olives are washed, ground into a paste, and the oil is
   extracted via mechanical decanters without the use of excessive heat or
   chemicals. [1 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>]
   - *Waste Management:* Olive waste (*alperujo*) is highly valued in the
   circular economy, often being composted for fertilizer, used as biomass =
for
   energy, or used in animal feed. [1
   <https://www.oliveoiltimes.com/business/europe/spains-olive-pomace-oil-i=
ndustry-gets-a-voice/50290>,
   2 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>]

3. Storage & Packaging

   - *Storage:* To maintain freshness, the oil is stored in massive, dark
   stainless steel tanks that are often blanketed with nitrogen to prevent
   oxidation.
   - *Bottling:* Over 1,500 bottlers process the raw oil before it enters
   retail or bulk distribution. [1
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DoD3Zg0d3T-s&t=3D1>, 2
   <https://oliveoilsfromspain.org/industry/>]

4. Logistics & Distribution

   - *Bulk vs. Bottled:* The supply chain is highly export-oriented. A
   significant portion of production (particularly for top destinations lik=
e
   Italy and Portugal) is transported in bulk utilizing specialized liquid
   logistics (like flexibags holding up to 24,000 liters in shipping
   containers). [1
   <https://www.msc.com/en/local-information/europe/spain/spain-olive-oil>,
   2
   <https://www.caixabankresearch.com/en/sectoral-analysis/agrifood/spanish=
-olive-oil-liquid-gold-must-be-developed-further>,
   3 <https://oec.world/en/profile/bilateral-product/olive-oil/reporter/esp=
>,
   4
   <https://sustainablefoodtrust.org/news-views/the-supply-chain-of-fats-ol=
ive-oil/>
   ]
   - *International Brands:* High-end bottled products are shipped directly
   to markets like the USA, Mexico, and the UAE by major companies like
   *Atasur* and *La Espa=C3=B1ola*. [1
   <https://oec.world/en/profile/bilateral-product/olive-oil/reporter/esp>,
   2 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DMoPqPsebq28&t=3D1>]

5. Key Market & Supply Chain Challenges

   - *Climate Volatility:* The Spanish olive oil supply chain is highly
   vulnerable to extreme heat and prolonged droughts in Southern Europe.
   Consecutive years of poor production have occasionally forced Spain to
   import oil from countries like Portugal and Tunisia to meet global deman=
d.
   [1
   <https://www.oliveoiltimes.com/business/europe/olive-oil-exports-from-sp=
ain-reach-record-high-defying-production-hurdles/135898>,
   2
   <https://www.shop.bottegadelsarto.com/feed/global-olive-oil-supply-chain=
-challenges-776804>,
   3 <https://oec.world/en/profile/bilateral-product/olive-oil/reporter/esp=
>
   ]
   - *Price Volatility:* Prices at origin can fluctuate dramatically,
   creating strain along the supply chain. Retail pricing models sometimes
   lag, squeezing profit margins for smaller producers. [1
   <https://www.oliveoiltimes.com/business/europe/olive-oil-exports-from-sp=
ain-reach-record-high-defying-production-hurdles/135898>,
   2
   <https://newmedit.ciheam.org/2025/06/10/distribution-strategies-in-the-v=
alue-chain-of-spanish-virgin-olive-oils/>,
   3
   <https://www.cde.unibe.ch/insights__media/blogs/coffee_corner/in_the_hea=
rt_of_empty_spain_the_uncertain_future_of_olive_oil/index_eng.html>,
   4
   <https://sustainablefoodtrust.org/news-views/the-supply-chain-of-fats-ol=
ive-oil/>,
   5
   <https://www.persistencemarketresearch.com/market-research/europe-olive-=
oil-market.asp>
   ]

Explore the broader structure and economic weight of the industry through
the Olive Oils from Spain <https://oliveoilsfromspain.org/industry/>
portal, or analyze global trade metrics using the Observatory of Economic
Complexity
<https://oec.world/en/profile/bilateral-product/olive-oil/reporter/esp>
database.
If you are researching a specific part of the chain, would you like
information on:

   - The *export destinations* and global trade volumes?
   - *Sustainable farming* and supply chain certifications?
   - How recent *climate disruptions* affected crop yields?


